{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 120, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed (expts 11,15,18-20) gives far larger gains than swapping out an existing op on edge 3 (expts 12-14)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, removing edge 3 leaves only the edge-5 path to the output, so the network can nearly collapse (expt 68: -75 on C10)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When node 1 has no direct route to the output, deleting edge 5 cuts all deep computation from the output (expts 72,73 vs 71,74-76)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the edge-3 shortcut, edge 5 may be one of very few routes to the output, so removing it is much more damaging (expt 73)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 1 is absent, removing edge 0 disconnects nodes 1 and 2 from the input entirely (expts 29,30: about -15 IN16 vs about -2 otherwise)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a node1-to-output conv path helps more when the output lacks the direct edge-3 input (expt 38 vs 31,39)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 4 partially replaces the missing input-to-output residual, which gives large gains especially on ImageNet16 (expts 95,96 vs 91-94)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is absent, replacing the edge-4 conv with skip removes the main remaining deep path into 